      "id": "UFEP-F-001",
      "note": "CEP-007 IV.2 requires eligibility to be decidable and V.2 requires every precondition to be machine-verifiable. Nothing in the repository measured them together, and one of the five — an accepted ratification — could not be measured at all because the registry CEP-006 mandates did not exist. Closed by measuring all five from the located determinations and machine models that own them, and by treating an unreadable source as unsatisfied per V.4.",
      "owner": "00-MASTER/UCOS-UFEP-001/ufep-declaration.json",
      "title": "Freeze eligibility was undecidable because no programme measured the CEP-007 Article V preconditions"
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "class": "DECLARED-SCOPE-BOUNDARY",
      "disposition": "GOVERNED",
      "evidence": [
        "00-CEP/STAGE-04-S4-12-INFRASTRUCTURE-005-UIMM-INTEGRATION-PROVISIONAL-RATIFICATION.md",
        "00-CEP/STAGE-04-S4-06-INFRASTRUCTURE-013-SECURITY-RATIFICATION-AND-INFRASTRUCTURE-014-NEXT-FRONTIER-DETERMINATION.md"
      ],
      "id": "UFEP-F-002",
      "note": "Band freeze requires a band certification-of-certifications step that a located determination records as the next lawful frontier and as not yet performed. That is a different scope from the per-artifact eligibility CEP-007 Article IV defines, and it is owned by the Band-13 programme. This programme's determination is explicitly scoped to the artifacts holding canonical ratification records, and it neither absorbs nor contradicts the band-scope determination.",
      "owner": "00-CEP/STAGE-04-S4-12-INFRASTRUCTURE-005-UIMM-INTEGRATION-PROVISIONAL-RATIFICATION.md",
      "title": "A located determination records BAND-scope freeze as NOT READY; that scope is not closed here"
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "class": "DECLARED-SCOPE-BOUNDARY",
      "disposition": "GOVERNED",
      "evidence": [
        "00-CEP/CEP-007-CONSTITUTIONAL-FREEZE-CONSTITUTION.md",
        "00-MASTER/UCOS-CRAT-001/07-FOUNDATION-FREEZE-AUTHORIZATION.md"
      ],
      "id": "UFEP-F-003",
      "note": "CEP-007 VII.1 reserves the freeze decision to Freeze Authority and I.5 forbids its self-conferral by Execution Authority. Every state past eligibility is declared unreachable by this programme and a self-guard fails closed if any subject is reported in one. The located freeze authorization is recorded as evidence that the authorization channel is occupied; it is not acted upon here.",
      "owner": "00-CEP/CEP-007-CONSTITUTIONAL-FREEZE-CONSTITUTION.md",
      "title": "Eligibility is not a freeze, and this programme cannot become one"
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "class": "DECLARED-SCOPE-BOUNDARY",
      "disposition": "GOVERNED",
      "evidence": [
        "00-CEP/CEP-006-CONSTITUTIONAL-RATIFICATION-CONSTITUTION.md",
        "09-DR-RAT-11-ASSESSMENT.md",
        "00-MASTER/UCOS-CRAT-001/07-FOUNDATION-FREEZE-AUTHORIZATION.md"
      ],
      "id": "UFEP-F-004",
      "note": "CEP-006 I.4 caps every in-corpus determination at provisional acceptance pending an out-of-corpus finality authority, and the located freeze authorization records that this standing condition is carried forward and is not a freeze blocker. Constitutional completion as determined here therefore means: every constitutional condition the repository is competent to decide is decided, measured, owned and gated. It does not mean, and must never be read as, constitutional finality.",
      "owner": "00-CEP/CEP-006-CONSTITUTIONAL-RATIFICATION-CONSTITUTION.md",
      "title": "Constitutional completion is completion of the machinery, not constitutional finality"
    },
    {
      "blocking": false,
      "class": "DECLARED-SCOPE-BOUNDARY",
      "disposition": "GOVERNED",
      "evidence": [
        "00-MASTER/UCCEP-000000/uccep-bindings.json",
        "00-MASTER/UCCEP-000000/uccep.json"
      ],
      "id": "UFEP-F-005",
      "note": "This programme reads the aggregate certifier's sealed model to decide three of its completion criteria. Binding its determination as a check inside that certifier would make the certifier a component of its own input, reproducing the recursion topology this repository forbids elsewhere. Only this programme's SELF-guards are bound there, as G-21. The determination itself is gated by its own Makefile target and CI workflow, which run the certifier at full tier first — and criterion UFEP-CC-11 measures that the model it read was in fact a full-tier one, so a tier-limited model cannot silently produce a completion verdict.",
      "owner": "00-MASTER/UCCEP-000000/uccep-bindings.json",
      "title": "The completion determination is downstream of the aggregate certifier and is deliberately not one of its checks"
    }
  ],
